TYPE=string
GROUP=round
DOC=SPIRA_ROUND_VM_SPILL — empty (off), `ec2`, `ec2-always` or `ec2-only`: `ec2` spills a round pass to EC2 when the hypervisor has no room or is io-bound; `ec2-always` leases every pass on EC2 first and falls back to the hypervisor only when EC2 cannot be acquired; `ec2-only` is `ec2-always` with no fallback — a pass whose EC2 acquire fails is an error. Production stays off until the operator turns it on.
SCHEMA=Round-VM spill provider: empty means rounds only ever run on the local hypervisor; `ec2` lets a pass spill to EC2 when the hypervisor has no room; `ec2-always` places every pass on EC2, falling back to local only if EC2 cannot be acquired; `ec2-only` never falls back.
